// Pixel art as data: one character per pixel, '.' is clear, every other
// character is a palette key. Authored with a scratch generator, then
// committed as plain grids: edit the rows here directly.
//
// Chapter 3-3, Over the Tracks: the station, the footbridge, the trains
// under it. Same layout as the rooftop set so the chunk baker works
// unchanged: tiles are 16 x 16, anchor top left, each kind one anim whose
// frames are variants (fps 0, pick by column hash). roofTop is the concrete
// platform edge with its yellow tactile strip, roofEdgeLeft and
// roofEdgeRight its ends, roofFill concrete with conduit (variant 1 a
// weep hole with a rust stain, variant 2 a junction box with a status light; weight the
// plain one heaviest), oneWay the see-through steel grating of the
// footbridge deck on its weathering steel edge beam, stone a cast concrete
// pier block, spikes snapped rail ends jutting from a sleeper, one still
// arcing (hazard), brick a battered orange equipment case (breakable),
// auraBlock the sigma crate in rail-yard steel, vent a platform grille with
// a status light, pipe two overhead conduits in a strut hanger.
//
// Decor anchor is the bottom left (y is the top of the floor row it stands
// on). signal: frame 0 red lit (lamp centre (8, 4)), frame 1 green lit
// (lamp centre (8, 10)); fps 0, pick the frame from World.signals[i].green.
// Light sources, in decor pixels from the top left: gantry the signal heads
// along row 19 (centre x 30); stationLamp the head at (9, 13); glassStairs
// the lit enclosure, centre (14, 11); platformSign the lightbox, centre (24,
// 8), it is the breakable L sign here (frame 0 on, frame 1 flicker);
// goalBridgeEnd the rail lights round (15, 27), 4 frames of the lights
// chasing, loop.
//
// ORANGE_TRAIN (128 x 34) and COMMUTER_TRAIN (128 x 42): cab and headlights
// on the right (mirror for dir -1). Row 2 is the roof line she stands on;
// the two rows above it are roof equipment. anchor (0, 2) is the vehicle's
// roof-top-left, the point World.vehicles gives as (x, y), so the body
// under it fills the sim's 8 x 2 (orange) and 8 x 2.5 (commuter) tile box.
//
// TRACKS_GLOW lists the keys that glow: S T O amber and warm, K F D C
// fluorescent and cool, R red, Z Y green, W white, M V the aura sigma, and
// the halos I L * % & @.
//
// TRACKS_BACKDROP: three 512 px tileable strips for the parallax, bottom on
// the horizon (the bottom row is solid, so it can be lifted). far (96): the
// city beyond under a late night sky, the boxy tower with its lit crown and
// the blue glass slab small in the distance. mid (96): the signature: the
// curved glass science building wrapped in bronze fins, lit warm inside
// with its atrium and spiral stair, the ribbed lab block beside it, and the
// rust-brown footbridge cresting over the tracks with lights in its rail.
// near (64): the station canopy, its columns and strip lights, overhead
// wires and the platform fence.
import type { Grid, Palette, SpriteSet } from './types';
import type { RooftopTile } from './rooftop';

